    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d537">

                <pb facs="1292" n="1178" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg1178"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President Roosevelt
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">most secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>,<anchor n="1"
                            xml:id="d537-f1"/>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-26">26 August
                        1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>414. Colonel Warden to President Roosevelt
                    personal and most secret most immediate.</p>
                <p>Should like to arrive Washington Wednesday 1st in time for dinner instead of
                    Monday 30th. Hope this will not be inconvenient to you. I feel I require a
                    little more rest. Will this be all right.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d537-f1" n="1" xml:id="d537-f1-content">
                <p>The message originated in Canada but was transmitted to Washington via London. It
                    was forwarded by the White House Map Room to Roosevelt, who was then at Hyde
                    Park, in telegram No. 
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">White</hi>
                     130, August 26, 1943.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
